module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.undeclared_transport_rendered_as_a_call_to_an_undeclared_function

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data undeclared_transport_rendered_as_a_call_to_an_undeclared_function: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "undeclared_transport_rendered_as_a_call_to_an_undeclared_function" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "native effect admission refusing, at compile, an entry whose demanded service operation declares no transport, so an operation with no realization is unreachable from an accepted native program rather than refused when invoked" } },

  receipts: [
    "**an operation whose service declares no transport is emitted as a call to a function nothing declares** (INVALID STATE: the bare transport node the parser and v1.compiler.emit emit_transport_node supply for an ABSENT transport was classified LocalTransport and bound to LocalBound, and every target rendered it as a direct call to a function named after the operation, with no arguments: Rust `Ok(start_detached())`, Python `return start_detached()`, Go `return StartDetached(), nil`.",

    "HARM: the function exists nowhere, so any crate whose closure reaches such a service fails rustc E0425 even when nothing calls the operation (extdeps.posix.process posix.Process StartDetached and Reap on the rfm-rung-census route, class 4 of stern-bat-401's emitter-debt list). It is fabricated output, absence read as a meaning (DESIGN section 5), and its cost is loud here only because the name happens not to exist.",

    "ROOT CAUSE (DESIGN section 6b): the earliest unjustified boundary was the transport classifier in v1.std.core (classify_transport), which named the absent-transport node LocalTransport, and the dispatch that gave that name a meaning. The census found 10 transport-less operations in 4 services (extdeps.posix.process, gunbc.code_change_workflow, gunbc.pr_digests, gunbc.review_verdict) and no same-named function for any of them: the local meaning had no legitimate user. DESIGN section 3: extdeps owns an operation's interface, and a transport is one of N handlers bound to it, so a transport-less operation is an interface whose realization this target is not given.",

    "REPAIRED: the node is UndeclaredTransport (undeclared_transport_node, is_undeclared_transport), it binds to UnboundOperation, and every target renders emit_unbound_operation_refusal: one error expression through the shared template, naming the operation and the target. The three fabricated local-call renderers and the dispatch's render_local parameter are deleted. RED/control: test.claim.unbound_operation_refusal_witness undeclared_transport_operation_refuses_by_name.",

    "RUNG: found at mitigatable (rustc refused the crate); still mitigatable after the repair, because the refusal fires when the operation is INVOKED (a panic naming it), not when a program that demands it is accepted. Ceiling structurally guaranteed through native effect admission refusing the demand at compile; climbable but unbuilt.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit", decl_name: "emit_unbound_operation_refusal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.emit", decl_name: "bind_operation_transport", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.unbound_operation_refusal_witness", decl_name: "undeclared_transport_operation_refuses_by_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
